text:
yasmin: Need a compact deprecation/migration snippet for the v1->v2 docs focused on runtime fallbacks and model-alias swaps. Target: single para guidance + one TS + one Py snippet + one curl smoke line + support ticket template. Keep it copy-light and safe. Who can own?

derek: I can. Will keep examples minimal and explicit about when to trigger fallback (5xx/network only) and a bold embedding-dim warning. Will also add a tiny GH Action job to run the curl smoke test.

derek: Draft paragraph: "When migrating from redwood-v1 to redwood-v2, run a canary on a subset of traffic and validate outputs against your eval set. Implement an availability fallback that triggers only on network/5xx errors to avoid masking client/auth failures. If you use embeddings, verify vector dimensionality before swapping models; re-encode or pin to the compatible model to avoid retrieval regressions."

marco: Good. Add a short sentence: "If deterministic outputs are required, pin to redwood-v1 until v2 is validated on your dataset."

build-bot: lint: ok. Suggest not catching generic Exception in examples; show pattern matching on status or error class. Also add a tiny telemetry comment like `// emit metric: migration_fallback_total`.

derek: TS snippet (tiny):
```ts
import { Client } from '@redwood/inference'
const c = new Client()
async function generate(prompt){
  try { return await c.generate({ model: 'redwood-v2', input: prompt }) }
  catch (e:any) {
    if (e.status && e.status >= 500) {
      // emit metric: migration_fallback_total
      return c.generate({ model: 'redwood-v1', input: prompt })
    }
    throw e
  }
}
```

derek: Py snippet (tiny):
```py
from redwood import Client
c = Client()
def generate(prompt):
    try:
        return c.generate(model='redwood-v2', input=prompt)
    except Exception as e:
        if getattr(e, 'status', 0) >= 500:
            # send telemetry: migration_fallback_total
            return c.generate(model='redwood-v1', input=prompt)
        raise
```

derek: One-line curl smoke test for GH Action:
```
curl -sS -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/generate -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" -d '{"model":"redwood-v2","input":"ping"}' || curl -sS -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/generate -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" -d '{"model":"redwood-v1","input":"ping"}'
```

ops: Support template to paste into tickets: "Observed availability fallback from redwood-v2 to redwood-v1 for request <request_id> at <timestamp>. Attach sample prompt/output, indicate whether embeddings were used, and whether the customer re-ran against pinned v1. Recommended next step: rerun sample against pinned v1 for deterministic comparison."

support: Please add a short admonition above embedding examples: "Warning: embedding dimension mismatch may break retrieval; verify dimensions before swapping models." Make it prominent.

derek: Will add the admonition and update redirect map + changelog note. Opening PR now: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4999 (contains paragraph, snippets, curl smoke test, GH Action job, telemetry note, and support template).

marco: Quick editorial nit: replace 'fallback' with 'availability fallback' in the paragraph to be explicit. Also prefer 're-encode vectors' phrasing over 're-index' for clarity.

derek: Edited per feedback and pushed. build-bot: can you run docs lint + smoke action?

build-bot: CI started: docs lint ✅, smoke-test action retried once due to transient 429 and passed on retry.

yasmin: Thanks team 680. I'll merge when green and ask #support to watch for increased fallback rates tomorrow morning. Keep the section concise; we don't want to bloat the migration guide.
